      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{64873f159cf028090ce2c2e2|full_name}: Here is a sample ID that does it: avtr_6d8676ff-6ac6-4bd8-9b79-95af4ba600fe\n\nThe setup in unity to cause something like this is to have a object that is small by default, but frame 1 of the animator running it becomes massive. From what I can tell, the nameplate location gets calculated not upon immediate avatar load, but once the animator starts running. The solution is keeping the object small for a few frames and THEN scaling it up, allowing the client to calculate the correct nameplate position",
